## Step 2 — Organize the header with Flexbox

The brand and navigation need to stay aligned while still wrapping on a narrow screen.

### 1. Turn the header into a flex container

```css
.site-header {
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: space-between;
  gap: 1rem;
  padding-block: 1rem;
}
```

### 2. Align the brand and navigation content

```css
.brand,
nav {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.75rem;
}
```

### 3. Style the brand

Use:

```css
.brand {
  font-weight: 800;
  text-decoration: none;
}
```

### 4. Let the navigation wrap

Add `flex-wrap: wrap` to `nav`.

### 5. Clean up the navigation links

For `nav a`, use `text-decoration: none` and `font-weight: 650`.

### What you should see

On a wide screen, the brand and links should sit across the header. On a narrow screen, the links may wrap onto another line instead of overflowing.

