quizDraft.prompt:
## Step 4 — Create reusable surfaces and form controls

The layout works, but the cards and registration form still look like plain document content.

### 1. Create one shared surface style

```css
.event-card,
.schedule-card,
.speaker-card,
.hero-note,
.registration-form {
  background: var(--surface);
  border-radius: var(--radius);
  padding: var(--space);
  box-shadow: var(--shadow);
}
```

### 2. Style the primary actions

```css
.button-link,
button {
  display: inline-block;
  border: 0;
  border-radius: 0.7rem;
  background: var(--accent);
  color: #ffffff;
  padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
  font: inherit;
  font-weight: 750;
  text-decoration: none;
  cursor: pointer;
}
```

### 3. Lay out the registration form

Use `display: grid`, `gap: 0.75rem`, and `max-width: 40rem` on `.registration-form`.

### 4. Style the form controls

```css
input,
select,
textarea {
  width: 100%;
  padding: 0.75rem;
  border: 1px solid #cbd5e1;
  border-radius: 0.6rem;
  font: inherit;
}
```

### What you should see

Cards and the form should share the same white surface, rounded corners, spacing, and shadow. The primary action should look like a blue button instead of a plain text link.

