## Step 5 — Add a wide-screen hero layout

The mobile layout already works because the content flows in one column. Keep that mobile layout as the default.

### Add one mobile-first breakpoint

```css
@media (min-width: 48rem) {
  .hero {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 2fr) minmax(14rem, 1fr);
    align-items: center;
    gap: 2rem;
  }

  main {
    padding-block: 3rem 5rem;
  }
}
```

The first hero column gets about twice the available space of the second. The second column will not shrink below `14rem`.

### What you should see

Below `48rem`, the hero should stay in one column.

At `48rem` and wider, the introduction and festival-details panel should sit side by side.

